  "overviews": [
    {
      "kind": "module",
      "name": "CARDDEMO",
      "key_points": [
        "The core credit-card management application: CICS screens for sign-on, accounts, cards, transactions, bill pay and reporting, plus the user-administration functions, over VSAM files.",
        "Its CARDDEMO CSD group installs 18 transactions; the batch behind them is exported as Control-M folders and a CA 7 listing in app/scheduler.",
        "The estate is AWS's mainframe modernization showcase - the repository states it exists to test discovery, migration and service-enablement approaches, not to run a real card portfolio."
      ],
      "basis": [
        "README.md:7",
        "app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD:1",
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:3",
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.ca7:19"
      ],
      "written_by": "agent"
    },
    {
      "kind": "chain",
      "name": "CARDDEMO",
      "key_points": [
        "The CA 7 job listing for the estate: the jobs the CA 7 export orders under the CARDDEMO application, including PAUTH's CBPAUP0J.",
        "It is the CA 7 view of the same estate the Control-M folders schedule - the two exports are alternative scheduler definitions shipped side by side."
      ],
      "basis": [
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.ca7:19",
        "store/CARDDEMO/schedule.json"
      ],
      "written_by": "agent"
    },
    {
      "kind": "chain",
      "name": "DAILY-TransactionBackup",
      "key_points": [
        "The daily transaction backup: it closes the VSAM files to batch, backs the transaction file up, waits, then reopens the files to the online region.",
        "Ordered every day (DAYS=ALL), and strictly serial - each job's OUT condition is the next one's IN condition, so CLOSEFIL, TRANBKP, WAITSTEP and OPENFIL cannot overlap.",
        "The close/open pair around the backup is what makes the file quiesce: nothing in the chain runs while the region holds the file."
      ],
      "basis": [
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:3",
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:4",
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:9",
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:20"
      ],
      "written_by": "agent"
    },
    {
      "kind": "chain",
      "name": "WEEKLY-TransactionTypesDBRefresh",
      "key_points": [],
      "basis": [],
      "written_by": "agent"
    },
    {
      "kind": "chain",
      "name": "DisclosureGroupsRefresh",
      "key_points": [
        "The weekly disclosure-group refresh: it closes the files, reloads the disclosure-group reference data and reopens the region.",
        "A Control-M SMART table ordered on Saturdays (DAYS=SA) inside the WEEKLY-TransactionTypesDBRefresh folder, not a standalone daily job.",
        "It is the chain the DB2 transaction-type refresh gates: MNTTRDB2's OUT condition is what releases this table's work."
      ],
      "basis": [
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:32",
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:38",
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:27"
      ],
      "written_by": "agent"
    },
    {
      "kind": "chain",
      "name": "TransactionTypesDBRefresh",
      "key_points": [],
      "basis": [],
      "written_by": "agent"
    },
    {
      "kind": "chain",
      "name": "MONTHLY-InterestCalculation",
      "key_points": [
        "The monthly interest run: it closes the files, calculates interest, combines the transaction files and reopens the region.",
        "Ordered as its own Control-M folder with the same close - work - wait - open shape as the daily backup.",
        "INTCALC is the accounting step of the month; COMBTRAN consolidates the transaction files it leaves behind."
      ],
      "basis": [
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:65",
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:69",
        "app/scheduler/CardDemo.controlm:75"
      ],
      "written_by": "agent"
    }
  ],
